# HR & Accounting SaaS (Pakistani Software Houses)

## Global rules (MUST FOLLOW)
- All business logic MUST be in backend. Frontend is UI only.
- Every table MUST have tenant_id (except users, tenants, tenant_users).
- NO delete on financial data — soft delete only.
- Payroll runs immutable once locked.
- Multi-tenancy enforced at DB level (RLS). Use `db.WithTenant` for tenant-scoped queries.
- All reports generated server-side. Flutter only consumes APIs.
- No biometric SDK in frontend. Start with MVP only — no overbuilding.

## Tech stack (fixed)
- **Backend**: Go, Fiber, JWT + Refresh Token, Redis (jobs), S3-compatible, server-side PDF.
- **Frontend**: Flutter Web/Desktop, Riverpod, pluto_grid, syncfusion_flutter_charts, go_router, Dio.
- **DB**: PostgreSQL, RLS, tenant_id on ALL tenant tables.

## Build order
1. Backend auth + tenant middleware ✓
2. Employees API ✓
3. Attendance API
4. Payroll engine + Payslip PDF
5. Flutter UI
6. Accounting (journals, accounts)
7. Reports
8. Biometric (later)

## API base
- Auth: POST /auth/signup, /auth/login, /auth/refresh
- Employees: GET/POST /api/employees, GET/PUT/DELETE /api/employees/:id (soft delete)
- Protected routes use middleware: RequireAuth(secret) → TenantFromJWT → RequireTenant
- Tenant ID comes from JWT claims; RLS uses `app.tenant_id` set in `db.WithTenant`.

## Implement in small, testable steps. Ask before deviating.
